# `optim::OptimaExitFlag`

Why a run of `optima` stopped.

`OptimaState::exit_flag` is one of these. Only `Converged` (1) means the optimality and feasibility tests were met; `MaxIterations` (0) means the budget ran out with the point still improving; every negative value means the run ended for a reason that needs a decision: `Stopped` (−1) is a progress hook returning `true`, `NoFeasiblePoint` (−2) means no point satisfying the constraints was found, `ObjectiveTargetReached` (−3) means the objective fell below the `objective_limit`, `NonFiniteEvaluation` (−4) means the objective or a constraint returned NaN or infinity where the solver could not recover, `InvalidProblem` (−5) means a callback broke its contract, `NoProgress` (−6) means steps stopped making progress away from a solution, and `ConstraintStationary` (−7) means the point is stationary for the constraint violation but still infeasible. `OptimaState::message` and the stall category say more.

## Fields

### `Converged`

`enumerator`, default `1`.

Optimality and feasibility tests met.

### `MaxIterations`

`enumerator`, default `0`.

The iteration budget ran out.

### `Stopped`

`enumerator`, default `-1`.

A progress hook returned `true`.

### `NoFeasiblePoint`

`enumerator`, default `-2`.

No feasible point was found.

### `ObjectiveTargetReached`

`enumerator`, default `-3`.

The objective passed `objective_limit`.

### `NonFiniteEvaluation`

`enumerator`, default `-4`.

A callback returned NaN or infinity unrecoverably.

### `InvalidProblem`

`enumerator`, default `-5`.

A callback broke its contract (wrong shape or dtype).

### `NoProgress`

`enumerator`, default `-6`.

Steps stopped making progress.

### `ConstraintStationary`

`enumerator`, default `-7`.

Stationary for the violation but infeasible.

## Guidance

Read as `OptimaState::exit_flag`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

Converged and out-of-iterations runs.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });

  optim::OptimaOptions options;
  options.sequential_qp.max_iterations = 1;
  out.writeln("default :", optim::optima_exit_flag_name(optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), {}, disc).exit_flag));
  out.writeln("1 iter  :", optim::optima_exit_flag_name(optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, disc).exit_flag));
}
```

### Example 2

Stopped by a hook, and the numeric codes. The codes are the integer values of the enumerators.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const pluss::Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  const auto objective = [&](const pluss::Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); };
  const auto disc = optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() - 1.0; });

  optim::OptimaOptions options;
  options.progress_hook = [](const optim::OptimaProgressSnapshot &) { return true; };
  const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, disc);
  out.writeln("exit =", optim::optima_exit_flag_name(result.exit_flag), "=", static_cast<int>(result.exit_flag));
}
```

### Example 3

An infeasible problem: the constraint `x² + 1 ≤ 0` can never hold. The run cannot converge and ends with a failure flag (here `NoProgress`: the steps stop getting closer to feasibility).

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const optim::OptimaState result = optim::optima([](const pluss::Series &x) { return x.square().sum(); }, pluss::series::make({1.0}), {},
      optim::constraints().nl_ineq([](const Pack &p) { return p.at("x").square().sum() + 1.0; }));
  out.writeln("converged =", result.converged, ", exit =", optim::optima_exit_flag_name(result.exit_flag));
}
```

